                "cache_hit": false,
                "api_called": true,
                "summary": "- The Church of the Holy Family in Binondo, Manila is also known as the Minor Basilica and National Shrine of San Lorenzo Ruiz and Our Lady of the Most Holy Rosary Parish.\n- It is under the jurisdiction of the Archdiocese of Manila and was founded by the Dominican Order in 1596 to serve Chinese converts to Christianity.\n- The current granite church was completed in 1852 and features a pagoda-like bell tower reflecting the Chinese cultural influence.\n- The church was elevated to the status of a Minor Basilica by Pope John Paul II in 1992 and became a National Shrine in 2024.\n- It has a rich history of destruction and reconstruction, surviving British bombardment in 1762 and significant damage during World War II.\n- Masses are conducted in multiple languages, including Tagalog, Mandarin, Hokkien, and English, reflecting the diverse community it serves.",
